line	
line	<str>Talk to Lazim and pick any head (remember which head you picked).</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine two 5&nbsp;kg pieces of granite (not sandstone!). (Ironmen: Mine a 3rd piece of any size for King's Ransom)</str>
line	
line	<str>Make the head you chose (if you don't make the head you chose, you will have to make another head). The other 5&nbsp;kg granite piece is used later.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you did not bring clay or coal, mine some now.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him and you'll fall into a temple.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Lazim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your chisel on the fallen statue four times to get all its limbs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Lazim again to retrieve the statue head.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take-sigil from the pedestal south of Lazim to get the M sigil.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go around all the rooms through the outer hallways and pick up the R, K and Z sigils. The matching limbs are automatically used and consumed to open the doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the centre room after collecting all four sigils</str>
line	
line	<str>Try to open the doors to place the sigils. Make sure to complete each dialogue.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use soft clay on the pedestal. (Cast a fire spell on the frozen fountain if you still need a water source.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a chisel on the 5&nbsp;kg granite.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the new stone head in the pedestal. The original head will be slightly too small. The new head should fit perfectly and trigger a cutscene (Make sure to finish dialogue).</str>
line	
line	<str>North-west: use your bread or cake or pie on Pentyn. You may have to right-click again on Pentyn to make sure you are using the food on him and not on the magic spell.</str>
line	
line	<str>North-east: cast wind bolt, blast, wave, or surge on the furnace.</str>
line	
line	<str>South-east: light the 6 braziers with the appropriate fuels.</str>
line	
line	<str>South-west: cast fire bolt, blast, wave, or surge on the fountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pass through the magic barrier and climb the ladder. (If you can't pass through barrier, talk to Lazim)</str>
line	
line	<str>Cast crumble undead on the boneguard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stone ladder to the south.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn on Protect from Melee and talk to the new boneguard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take 3 sandstones from the rubble pile.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Use a sandstone on the southern wall, then use your chisel on the wall. Repeat to completion.</col>
step	33	-	Quick guide step 33
line	<str>Talk to Lazim north-east of the quarry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring him 32&nbsp;kg of sandstone, it doesn't have to be all at once. You can break down big pieces with a chisel.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your chisel on the sandstone (32&nbsp;kg).</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the base on the flat ground.</str>
line	
line	<str>Repeat the process for a 20&nbsp;kg body.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your chisel on the statue.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Lazim and pick any head (remember which head you picked).</str>
line	
